          H3("Worked example: Little's Law"),
          "Little's Law links the three core flow metrics for a stable system: **average cycle time = average WIP ÷ average throughput**. Suppose a team averages 12 items in progress and finishes 4 items a week. Average cycle time is 12 ÷ 4 = 3 weeks. If the team lowers WIP to 8 items and throughput holds at 4 a week, average cycle time falls to 8 ÷ 4 = 2 weeks, with no one working harder. This is the reasoning behind [WIP limits](" + K + "wip-limits/). Use it to understand your system, not to forecast single items: it assumes a roughly stable system.",
